    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224-a5">

                <pb facs="0406" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg346"/>

                <head>Mr. de Varigny to Mr. Whittall.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Honolulu,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 10, 1867.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your course of action is most fully and
                    entirely approved of, and I am happy to tender to you the thanks of his Majesty
                    and cabinet for your prompt and energetic interference in behalf of our
                    flag.</p>
                <p>I write by this mail to our chargé d’affaires in Lima in relation to this
                    subject, and inform him of the dangers that might accrue to our good name from
                    an indiscriminate use of our flag. Instructions to this effect had already been
                    transmitted to him, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>I renew to you, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. DE VARIGNY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. W. Whittall,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">His Hawaiian Majesty</hi>’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Consul General for Hong Kong and Macao.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
